		<h1 class="fw-bold text-center text-black text-uppercase" style="font-family: 'Source Sans 3', Helvetica, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.4rem; font-weight: 800 !important;" id="tank-types">Tank Types</h1>
		<div class="row mt-5 mb-5">
		  <div class="row">
		    <h4 class="fw-bolder text-uppercase text-black">Freshwater Tanks</h4>
		  </div>
		  <div class="row">
		    <div class="col-4 text-black">
		      <ul>
			<li><b>Ease of Maintenance:</b> Freshwater aquariums are generally easier to set up and maintain compared to saltwater tanks. They require less specialized equipment and are often more forgiving when it comes to water quality.</li>
			<li><b>Diverse Species:</b> With a wide range of fish and plant species available, freshwater aquariums offer plenty of options for customization and creativity. </li>
			<li><b>Cost-Effective:</b> Freshwater fish tend to be less expensive than their marine counterparts, making it a budget-friendly choice for new aquarium enthusiasts </li>
			<li><b>Stunning Plant Life:</b> Freshwater aquariums allow for beautiful aquatic plants, enhancing the aesthetic appeal and providing natural filtration. </li>
		      </ul>
		    </div>
		    <div class="col images" id="img5"></div>
		  </div>
		</div>

		<div class="row mt-5">
		  <div class="row">
		    <h4 class="fw-bolder text-uppercase text-black">Maringe - Fish only (FOT) Tank</h4>
		  </div>
		  <div class="row">
		    <div class="col-4 text-black">
		      <ul>
			<li><b>Vibrant Colors:</b> Marine fish are known for their striking colors and patterns, creating a visually stunning display that can brighten any space </li>
			<li><b>Engaging Behavior:</b>Many marine fish exhibit interesting behaviors, providing an engaging viewing experience for you and your guests </li>
			<li><b>Ease of Maintenance:</b> Marine fish aquariums often come with artificial coral or live rocks, which are easier to set up and maintain. Marine fish require less specialized equipment and are often more forgiving when it comes to water quality compared to coral. </li>
		      </ul>
		    </div>
		    <div class="col images" id="img6"></div>
		  </div>
		</div>

		<div class="row mt-5">
		  <div class="row">
		    <h4 class="fw-bolder text-uppercase text-black">Marine - Reef Tank</h4>
		  </div>
		  <div class="row">
		    <div class="col-4 text-black">
		      <ul>
			<li><b>Biodiversity:</b> Reef aquariums support a diverse range of marine life, including corals, fish, and invertebrates. This creates a dynamic and vibrant ecosystem </li>
			<li><b>Natural Beauty:</b>The combination of live corals and colorful fish creates a breathtaking underwater landscape that mimics natural reef environments.  </li>
			<li><b>Fascinating Interactions:</b> The interactions between different species in a reef aquarium can be captivating to observe, offering insights into the complexities of marine life.</li>
			<li><b>Sustainability:</b> Many reef aquarium setups can incorporate sustainable practices, such as using aquacultured corals and fish, promoting conservation.</li>
		      </ul>
		    </div>
		    <div class="col images" id="img7"></div>
		  </div>
		</div>
		
		<div class="row mt-5">
		  <div class="row">
		    <h4 class="fw-bolder text-uppercase text-black">Marine - Jellyfish Tank</h4>
		  </div>
		  <div class="row">
		    <div class="col-4 text-black">
		      <ul>
			<li><b>Unique Aesthetic:</b> Jellyfish aquariums are striking and mesmerizing, offering a one-of-a-kind focal point with their graceful movement and ethereal appearance.  </li>
			<li><b>Low Maintenence:</b>While jellyfish require specific care and specific design of aquarium, they generally need less daily maintenance than traditional fish aquariums, making them easier to manage. </li>
			<li><b>Fascinating Behavior:</b> Watching jellyfish swim and pulse through the water is a captivating experience, often serving as a conversation starter in any setting. </li>
			<li><b>Educational Appeal:</b> Jellyfish aquariums can provide valuable lessons about marine biology and the importance of jellyfish in ocean ecosystems.</li>
		      </ul>
		    </div>
		    <div class="col images" id="img8"></div>
		  </div>
		</div>
